[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Justice was Done]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.43]Lesson 35 | 第35课
[00:02.64]Justice was done | 正义得到伸张
[00:10.56]The word 'justice' is given two different meanings in the text. | “正义”一词在课文中有两种不同的含义。
[00:15.28]What is the distinction between them? | 它们之间的区别是什么？
[00:19.85]The word justice is usually associated with courts of law. | “正义”这个词通常与法庭联系在一起。
[00:25.49]We might say that justice has been done when a man's innocence or guilt has been proved beyond doubt. | 当我们说某人的无辜或罪行已被确凿地证实时，我们可以说正义得到了伸张。
[00:33.15]Justice is part of the complex machinery of the law. | 正义是复杂法律机器的一部分。
[00:37.75]Those who seek it, undertake an arduous journey and can never be sure that they will find it. | 寻求正义的人历尽艰辛，而且永远不能肯定能否找到正义。
[00:44.88]Judges, however wise or eminent, are human and can make mistakes. | 然而法官无论多么明智、多么杰出，毕竟是人，也会犯错误。
[00:51.18]There are rare instances when justice almost ceases to be an abstract concept. | 在罕见的情况下，正义几乎不再是抽象概念。
[00:58.16]Reward or punishment are meted out quite independent of human interference. | 奖惩的实施不受人为的干预。
[01:04.30]At such times, justice acts like a living force. | 在这种时候，正义像一种活的力量在起作用。
[01:09.44]When we use a phrase like 'it serves him right', | 当我们使用“他罪有应得”这句话时，
[01:13.51]we are, in part, admitting that a certain set of circumstances has enabled justice to act of its own accord. | 我们部分地承认了某种特定的环境使正义自发地起了作用。
[01:23.84]When a thief was caught on the premises of a large jewellery store one morning, | 一天早晨，一个小偷在一家大珠宝店里被人抓住，
[01:29.48]the shop assistants must have found it impossible to resist the temptation to say 'it serves him right'. | 店员们一定觉得很难抗拒说一句“他罪有应得”的诱惑。
[01:37.67]The shop was an old converted house with many large, disused fireplaces and tall, narrow chimneys. | 这家珠宝店是由一所旧房子改建的，屋里有许多废弃不用的巨大壁炉和又高又窄的烟囱。
[01:46.07]Towards midday, a girl heard a muffled cry coming from behind one of the walls. | 快到中午的时候，一个姑娘听见从一堵墙后传来闷乎乎的哭声。
[01:52.86]As the cry was repeated several times, | 由于这种叫声重复了几次，
[01:55.79]she ran to tell the manager who promptly rang up the fire brigade. | 她跑去告诉经理，经理立即给消防队打了电话。
[02:01.37]The cry had certainly come from one of the chimneys, | 哭声肯定来自烟囱，
[02:04.65]but as there were so many of them, the firemen could not be certain which one it was. | 但由于烟囱太多，消防队员不能确定是哪一个。
[02:12.25]They located the right chimney by tapping at the walls and listening for the man's cries. | 他们敲击墙壁倾听哭声，从而确定了正确的烟囱。
[02:19.67]After chipping through a wall which was eighteen inches thick, | 他们凿透一堵18英寸厚的墙之后，
[02:24.23]they found that a man had been trapped in the chimney. | 发现有个人被困在了烟囱里。
[02:28.40]As it was extremely narrow, the man was unable to move, | 由于烟囱极其狭窄，那人无法动弹，
[02:33.21]but the fire fighters were eventually able to free him by cutting a huge hole in the wall. | 但消防队员最终通过在墙上凿开一个大洞把他解救了出来。
[02:40.91]The sorry-looking, blackened figure that emerged, | 那个满脸愁容、浑身漆黑的家伙爬出来之后，
[02:44.98]admitted at once that he had tried to break into the shop during the night but had got stuck in the chimney. | 立刻承认他夜里企图进店行窃，却卡在了烟囱里。
[02:53.22]He had been there for nearly ten hours. | 他在里面待了将近10个小时。
[02:57.25]Justice had been done even before the man was handed over to the police. | 在那人被交送警察之前，正义就已得到了伸张。
